Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 01:19:24 +0900
Subject: [clangd] Optional minidump capture on unhandled exceptions (Windows)

On Windows, clangd can write a minidump for an unhandled exception into a directory given on the command line, so a crash on a user's machine has a symbolized stack. The support library carries its public declaration.

* [clangd] Optional minidump capture on unhandled exceptions (Windows)

  Release builds print no usable stack on Windows without a debugger,
  which has kept the hard module-related crashes out of reach.

  Add --crash-dumps-dir: when set, an unhandled exception filter writes a
  minidump with full memory and thread stacks into the directory before
  the process terminates as it would have. The filter is process-wide and
  runs after LLVM's own diagnostics; the flag defaults to off and the
  implementation is compiled only on Windows.

* [clangd] Crash dump support carries its public declaration
